        {
          "id": 3202837071,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Are you thinking in addition to this or replacing this? Some of the suggestions sound more developer centric than user centric, but that's also why I wanted feedback from developers I thought may want the feature for their users.  Are your \"internal profiles\" already sitting on a server and you'd prefer users to just point to them, rather than copying it over to their setup during installation?  I see pluses and minuses to that approach (with the profiles potentially being dynamic). Is this solution too \"platform specific\", because some platforms like more flexibility on how/what to install? (I'll also take suggestions/improvements where it's obvious this MR didn't add the intended support for installation on a particular platform)\n\nAre you thinking that #16902 is the best long term goal, so solutions should be created to support that better?\n\nCurrently the profile dictates which preference file is loaded, so I'm not sure how that would work (am I missing something?).  Did you intentionally refer to \"preference (advanced)\" to be the \"recent\" and \"recent_common\" files Wireshark GUI produces?  If so, that eliminates TShark as a possibility to use this feature.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
